  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "RC \"Maze\"​ Solving Car Game",
    "description": "Designed a RC car that could be user-controlled or automated using a MSP430F5528, Pixy, RFID reader, and XBee.\nDesigned a track for this game.\nEverything from choosing what parts were needed and how they all interfaced with each other to designing the PCB and having it printed to soldering everything on, testing, coding, and more testing/debugging was done in this project.\n\nThe objective of the game is this car is trying to get from a starting point to an ending point. On the way to the ending point there are mines (LEDs) and checkpoints (RFIDs). So, the car has a gas value that slowly counts down when the game starts. When a mine is hit, the car loses gas. When a checkpoint is hit, the car gains gas. If the gas hits 0, you lose. If you reach the ending point before it hits 0, you win. There are several paths you can take to get to each checkpoint. One path may be easier than the other (path shorter, less mines). These LEDs were set at different frequencies to represent the mine as on when the LED was on and off when the LED was off. This car can scan the whole track and based on what it sees through the Pixy camera, it can choose the best route on its own and follow the paths to the end. This car can also be user-controlled in the sense that the user can tell the car which path to take and when to stop or go. Xbees were used for wireless communication between the car and the controller.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Aug 2016 - Dec 2016"
   },
   {
    "title": "1-D Time-Domain Convolution Project",
    "description": "Successfully created and interfaced parts together in code to accomplish 1-D time-domain convolution on a custom-created circuit on a Nallatech board that exploits a significant amount of parallelism to improve performance compared to a microprocessor.\n\nCreated components in VHDL include Datapath, Controller, Signal Buffer, Kernel Buffer, Glue Logic, and SRAMs.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Aug 2014 - Dec 2014"
   }
